# The vendored Asciidoctor stylesheets are embedded verbatim via `include_str!`
# and compared byte-for-byte against Asciidoctor's LF output, so they must stay
# LF on every platform — a CRLF checkout (e.g. Windows `core.autocrlf`) would
# embed `\r\n` and diverge from Asciidoctor (and the CodeRay copy asserts it
# carries no `\r`). The `ref/` copies are pinned too so the drift-guard tests
# (which read them back) see the same bytes. Everything else is left to each
# contributor's git defaults.
html5/assets/asciidoctor-default.css text eol=lf
ref/asciidoctor/data/stylesheets/asciidoctor-default.css text eol=lf
html5/assets/coderay-asciidoctor.css text eol=lf
ref/asciidoctor/data/stylesheets/coderay-asciidoctor.css text eol=lf

# The `adoc --help syntax` crib sheet is embedded via `include_str!` and the
# tests assert its exact bytes (it opens with `= AsciiDoc Syntax\n`), so it must
# stay LF too – a CRLF checkout would embed `\r\n` and break those assertions.
cli/assets/syntax.adoc text eol=lf
